{"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is the trie of the patterns with two more links per state: the failure link, to the state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the longest proper suffix of the state’s prefix that is also a prefix of some pattern, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the output link, to the nearest state along the failure links at which a pattern ends. A scan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"follows the trie while the text matches and the failure links where it stops matching, so it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads each symbol of the text once and reports all the matches in O("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"k","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") for a text of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols with "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"k","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" matches."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","for match in automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\") {","    print(match.patternIndex, match.range)","}","\/\/ 1 1..<4   (\"she\")","\/\/ 0 2..<4   (\"he\")","\/\/ 3 2..<6   (\"hers\")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matches come in order of where they end, and of those ending at one place, longest first."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Ranges count the text’s symbols from 0. The automaton is built once and is immutable."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Symbols are mapped to dense indices at construction, through a 256-entry table when they are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"UInt8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a dictionary otherwise, so a scan over bytes, such as a string’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"utf8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", does no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hashing. When the states times the distinct symbols are few enough, every transition is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"precomputed into a table, and a scan takes one load per symbol.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975)."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/Match","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/MatchesView","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifie